= Price impact — Technical =

Price impact can be modeled from the execution curve or order-book/AMM depth. In a constant-product AMM, finite trades move the reserve ratio nonlinearly; the average execution price therefore differs from the pre-trade marginal price, with the gap increasing as trade size becomes large relative to reserves.

== Modeling / security cautions ==
* price impact ≠ slippage
* price impact ≠ trading fee
* same spot price ≠ same market depth

== References ==
* Albert S. Kyle, “Continuous Auctions and Insider Trading” (1985), for market-depth/price-impact foundations.
* Uniswap Labs, “What is price impact?”, current documentation.
* BIS Working Paper 1062, “Systemic fragility in decentralised markets” (2022), on price impact of DeFi liquidations.
